    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1033">

                <pb facs="1420" n="1408" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg1408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.92/12–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Political Adviser in Siam</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Tost</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-12-22T16:00:00-05:00">December 22,
                            1945—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>80. Dept believes US should not resume diplomatic relations immediately on treaty
                    signing to avoid association therewith, but equally should avoid long delay.
                    Present view is that Jan 1 would be suitable day, but feel we must clear with
                    Brit so that both may act same day, but with US technically in advance in view
                    previous deferment. Please advise Dept immediately your judgment as to most
                    suitable time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
